<item>
            <title>[LU-20333] Associate nodemaps with exports on MGS side</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20333</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Currently, exports on server side are associated with a nodemap, thanks to a call to &lt;tt&gt;nodemap_add_member&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;at peer connect time (&lt;tt&gt;.o_connect&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;o_reconnect&lt;/tt&gt;). This is done for MDS and OSS servers, as nodemaps are primarily designed for identity mapping and user access control.&lt;br/&gt;
But the MGS could also leverage the nodemap feature, and implement access control based on nodemap properties. For this to work, exports on MGS side need to be associated with nodemaps.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
